# Quake III Arena retail game data — NEVER redistributable (v38.107). The GPL
# covers id's source and id's game bytecode, never pak0.pk3: the maps, textures,
# models and sounds in it belong to the retail release. Drop your own copy in
# assets/q3/pak0.pk3 (or point MECTOV_PAK0 at it) and scripts/q3a_data.py will
# stage what a map needs; neither the .pk3 nor the extracted tree may ever be
# committed. `build/` above already covers the extraction directory, these
# cover a copy dropped into the tree by hand. See README "Game data".
*.pk3
assets/q3/

# LAST RULE, ON PURPOSE: the vendored id Software tree (v38.105) ships
# verbatim, so nothing above may filter it. Its GPL COPYING.txt/README.txt and
# q3asm's .txt notes fall under `*.txt`, and it carries a build.sh — both would
# otherwise be silently dropped (last match wins in gitignore, so this has to
# come after every exclusion pattern).
!third_party/q3a/**
